Reason: draw_background_part and draw_background_part_ext handed the renderer the part exactly as asked, while the
sprite part draws clip it to the image first, as GameMaker does. AM2R's area 7 waterfalls (oWaterfall) draw
bgWaterfall, 64x128, in parts that run down to the water level, hundreds of rows taller than the image, so the
renderer read whatever sits below it on the texture page and added it on screen, moving with the falling water
(issue #3). The clip the two sprite part draws repeated now lives in one helper that the background parts share.
Upstream: Bug on every platform, still in upstream main on 2026-11-04 (16cc651).

